      "content": {
        "blurb": "A controlled searchbox starts empty with localized zero-configuration chrome.",
        "environment": {
          "locale": "en-US",
          "direction": "ltr",
          "theme": "light",
          "catalog": {
            "structural.search.placeholder": "Search inspections…",
            "structural.search.clear": "Clear search"
          }
        },
        "props": {
          "value": "{value}",
          "debounceMs": 200
        },
        "state": {
          "value": {
            "kind": "string",
            "initial": ""
          },
          "publications": {
            "kind": "array",
            "initial": []
          }
        },
        "body": [
          {
            "control": "raw",
            "react": "<SearchInput value={value} onChange={publish} placeholder={placeholder} debounceMs={debounceMs} />\n<output className=\"hl-gallery-activation\" aria-live=\"polite\">Published: {publications.length ? publications.join(' → ') || '(empty)' : 'none'}</output>",
            "blazor": "<HarborlineSearchInput Value=\"@value\" ValueChanged=\"Publish\" DebounceMs=\"@DebounceMs\" />\n<output class=\"hl-gallery-activation\" aria-live=\"polite\">Published: @PublishedText</output>\nprivate string PublishedText => publications.Count == 0 ? \"none\" : string.Join(\" → \", publications) is { Length: > 0 } text ? text : \"(empty)\";",
            "rationale": "SearchInput is a compound searchbox with generated localized clear and busy chrome plus debounced publication, while its sibling output conditionally renders none, joins every published value with an arrow, and substitutes (empty) when that join is empty; an input descriptor and the closed vocabulary cannot express that complete structure and behavior."
          }
        ],
        "footer": []
